{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Therefore.</b> Because of the borders concerning which Israel was warned. <b>It is said in the Book of the Wars of YHWH.</b> Many books have been lost from among us and are not available to us, such as the Chronicles of the Kings of Israel, and the songs of Solomon and his proverbs. Likewise they had a Book of the Wars of HaShem, in which they would write the names of the borders through which they passed, which were forbidden to provoke, and they called them 'Wars of HaShem' — as an analogy to what Abigail said to David: כי מלחמות יהוה אדני נלחם וגו׳. <b>It says.</b> The mem has a pathach." "<b>Et Vahev in Suphah.</b> Vahev is a place name, at the end of the border of the land of Moab through which Israel passed, like בסופה — את לאפום (at Alef-Beth) is interchangeable with שורק (at Shin-Resh-Qof), in the manner of מול סוף / מול הגלגל, and ותקח צפורה צור / הביטו אל צור, and חוצבתם כיום / אתמול כי ערוך מאתמול."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "The final phrase refers to a vowel point on the letter mem; rendered literally.", 1 "The argument demonstrates interchangeable word pairs from different root spellings; the citation fragments are rendered as they appear without expansion."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:03.818879069Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}